{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvaoEamP3bPc3FPoTqej","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I'd hold the launch, but I wouldn't run the non-buyer survey as the main next step.**\n\n**Why the survey is weak**\n- Stated willingness to pay is unreliable. People say a lower price would work far more often than they then buy.\n- Non-buyers are the group least able to tell you what would make the product worth buying.\n- The result is 10x below target, and 40% of buyers refunded. Price alone is unlikely to close a gap that size. The refunds suggest the offer's value or expectations were wrong, and a lower price wouldn't fix that.\n\n**What I'd do instead**\n1. **Check the funnel.** Find out how many people actually saw the offer, and how many clicked and reached checkout. A low-visibility placement and a weak product proposition look identical in a 0.3% figure.\n2. **Find out why buyers refunded.** Ask the refunders and the buyers who kept it. There are probably only about 30 buyers if the 20,000 were split evenly, so a few interviews will tell you a lot. Check whether the offer set expectations that the product didn't meet.\n3. **Test price with behaviour, not opinion.** If price is still the leading hypothesis, run a randomised test at two or three lower prices (say £5 and £9). It costs little and gives you real purchase and refund data.\n4. **Sanity-check the 3% target.** Ask what it was based on. Net of refunds, you're at about 0.18%.\n\n**Caveats**\n- Your sample of buyers is small, so the 40% refund rate is imprecise. It could be anywhere from about 25% to 58%.\n- If you do run the survey anyway, ask about the problems customers have and how they handle them today. Don't ask \"would you pay £X?\"\n\n**Decision rule:** Only proceed if a lower price shows both materially higher conversion and refunds well below 40%."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3203,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3203},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea3b7d30-d3aa-4fe7-8ab5-3efb3c5b173c","uuid":"bfd3e0c5-f5c8-431d-b4ce-f301c81c1193","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:10:17.125Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaoELdmZ5FCNY8ygsUC"}
